1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,096
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,096 --> 00:00:08,978
This morning the system named no pick, so tonight there is nothing to grade.

3
00:00:08,978 --> 00:00:13,700
No setup, no trade, no loss — that is the discipline working.

4
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:18,619
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

5
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:24,009
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

6
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:29,804
On the day, the book is down 289 dollars.

7
00:00:29,804 --> 00:00:33,460
Dollar Tree (DLTR) leads, +2.6 percent.

8
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:35,898
Target (TGT) lags at -1.8.

9
00:00:35,898 --> 00:00:40,960
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

10
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,443
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

11
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:54,073
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

12
00:00:54,073 --> 00:01:00,872
10 positions, led by Target, ticker TGT, Dollar Tree, ticker DLTR, 3M, ticker MMM.

13
00:01:00,872 --> 00:01:12,147
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

14
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:18,516
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

15
00:01:18,516 --> 00:01:20,954
Every morning OROS proposes.

16
00:01:20,954 --> 00:01:31,663
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

17
00:01:31,663 --> 00:01:35,668
Inside the book today: 5 positions up, 5 down.

18
00:01:35,668 --> 00:01:38,106
Best, DLTR at +2.62 percent.

19
00:01:38,106 --> 00:01:39,847
Worst, TGT at -1.80.

20
00:01:39,847 --> 00:01:44,897
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

21
00:01:44,897 --> 00:01:52,211
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -2.88% per trade over 1300 graded positions.

22
00:01:52,211 --> 00:01:59,350
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 50% position size.

23
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:04,574
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

24
00:02:04,574 --> 00:02:16,938
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 0 names close the day in Stage 2; position size stays cut to 50% until the record earns it back.

25
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:20,705
Over to the sports desk.

26
00:02:20,705 --> 00:02:30,046
Day 94 of the race: three books, the same one hundred thousand simulated dollars, since July sixth.

27
00:02:30,046 --> 00:02:36,368
In first place, the live self-rebuilding book, in blue, at 108,099.

28
00:02:36,368 --> 00:02:41,935
Then the index fund, in gray, 8.0 thousand back at 100,067.

29
00:02:41,935 --> 00:02:49,200
Then the frozen first portfolio, the green line, 8.8 thousand back at 99,281.

30
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:51,842
The race has no finish line.

31
00:02:51,842 --> 00:02:56,182
Same books, same dollars, back at it tomorrow.

32
00:02:56,182 --> 00:03:01,089
Every line starts the same day with the same dollar.

33
00:03:01,089 --> 00:03:02,976
Nothing is restated.

34
00:03:02,976 --> 00:03:11,846
On screen, three equity lines grown from the same starting dollar: the frozen first book, the live book, and the index fund.

35
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:20,880
All figures are simulated paper trading, graded and journaled by the OROS agents with no human intervention.

36
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:23,117
Nothing here is financial advice.

37
00:03:23,117 --> 00:03:26,099
From the closing desk — see you at the open.
